{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018oNgNxZgftyk3wERXFgQng","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# N40_CLI_CUTOVER result\n2\t\n3\tstatus: PASSED\n4\tnode_prompt: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompts/N40_cli_cutover.prompt.v1.md\n5\tpredecessor: N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS (compact state supplied by the controller, status PASSED)\n6\tgeneration: 1\n7\t\n8\t## What this node built\n9\t\n10\t- `runtime/run_curriculum.py` — rewritten from the Plan 25 `CurriculumRuntime`/\n11\t  `CurriculumFactoryGraph`/`CodexWorker` dispatcher into the sole production CLI\n12\t  described by spec section 16. It parses/validates the exact\n13\t  preflight/`--unit`/`--all`/`--resume` argument surface, canonicalizes\n14\t  `--engine-root`/`--curriculum`/`--output-root`, enforces the fresh-run\n15\t  collision rule and the resume-identity rule, acquires the per-output-root\n16\t  execution lock, calls `persistence.prepare_episode_invocation` once, builds\n17\t  `runtime.langgraph_factory.graph.build_curriculum_factory_graph` exactly once\n18\t  per execution path, invokes it, projects the returned `FactoryOutput` into the\n19\t  one printed JSON object, and maps the result to spec section 14's exit codes.\n20\t  It holds no node body, no guard, no join, no acceptance rule, and no frontier\n21\t  selection.\n22\t- `tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py` — 72 tests covering the node's own TEST\n23\t  checklist (below).\n24\t- `results/evidence/N40_CLI_CUTOVER/` — `focused_test_run.txt` (this node's exact\n25\t  verification command), `cli_help.txt` and `import_audit.txt` (regenerated by\n26\t  tests, not hand-written), `preflight_read_only.txt` and\n27\t  `plan25_resume_refusal.txt` (real, unmocked runs of `main()` against a real\n28\t  filesystem, captured as a test side effect so they can never drift from what\n29\t  actually passed).\n30\t\n31\t## Migration disposition\n32\t\n33\tThe GOAL explicitly allows historical modules to remain \"only when unreachable\n34\tfrom the production import/call graph.\" `runtime/run_curriculum.py` no longer\n35\timports `runtime.controller.CurriculumRuntime`, `runtime.curriculum_factory_graph\n36\t.CurriculumFactoryGraph`, `runtime.model_worker.CodexWorker`/`GeminiReviewer`, or\n37\t`runtime.session_bridge` — the entire Plan 25 dispatcher, the custom FSM\n38\t(`controller.simulate`), and the session bridge are all unreachable from the one\n39\tproduction entry point now. Those modules, and their own dedicated tests\n40\t(`tests/runtime/test_controller.py`, `test_curriculum_factory_graph.py`), are\n41\tleft in place as readable history, per the GOAL's \"do not delete user history.\"\n42\t\n43\t**One residual conflict, out of this node's write set.**\n44\t`tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py` is not in this node's declared writable\n45\tpaths and could not be touched. It tests the *old* `run_curriculum.parser_for`/\n46\t`main` API directly — mocking `runtime.run_curriculum.CurriculumFactoryGraph`\n47\tand asserting a `--lab-id` dispatch to `factory.run(...)`. That is precisely the\n48\tPlan 25 fallback path this node's GOAL requires removing, so the file now fails\n49\tto import (`cannot import name 'parser_for'`) against the new CLI. This node's\n50\town verification command\n51\t(`{python} -m pytest -q tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py\n52\ttests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py`) does not exercise that file and passes\n53\tcleanly; `pytest -q tests/runtime` (run by N50, per\n54\t`implementation.graph.v3.yaml`) will fail collection on it until a node with\n55\twrite access to `tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py` retires or rewrites it.\n56\tFlagging this explicitly rather than routing around it silently.\n57\t\n58\t**Graph topology inherited, not extended.** `build_curriculum_factory_graph`\n59\t(`runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py`, sha256\n60\t`eae00c21bfe55ce6e2d6c4374611db4d84d286218d498fa520e799288e152e26`, unchanged —\n61\tmatches N32's own receipted output hash exactly) wires the skeleton and the\n62\tper-unit fan-out path only; the unit-repair cycle (D16-D23) and the workbook\n63\tengine (D24-D32, `register_workbook_topology`) are not yet wired into the one\n64\tcompile point `binding_inventory()`'s own docstring documents this as N31's/\n65\tN32's deliberate deferral, not a regression this node introduced. `graph.py` is\n66\tnot in this node's write set, so a live run that reaches an unwired destination\n67\traises `KeyError`; the CLI's top-level `except Exception` catches it and prints\n68\ta `SYSTEM_FAILURE`-shaped object with exit 20, never a fabricated success. This\n69\tis the correct, honest behavior for the graph's current state, not a workaround.\n70\t\n71\t## TEST checklist, item by item\n72\t\n73\t1. **Static and runtime call-graph proof shows one production graph\n74\t   builder/path.** `ImportGraphAuditTests` parses the CLI's own AST and asserts\n75\t   no Plan 25/legacy module or symbol is imported, and that\n76\t   `build_curriculum_factory_graph` is the only builder referenced (no\n77\t   `register_skeleton`/`register_workbook_topology`/`.compile(` call). The\n78\t   runtime side: `FreshRunWiringTests` monkeypatches the builder with a counting\n79\t   stub and asserts exactly one call for a fresh run; `Plan25ResumeRefusalTests`\n80\t   and `CapabilityAndAuthorizationFailureTests` assert **zero** calls when the\n81\t   run is refused before an episode.\n82\t2. **CLI help exposes no legacy path.** `HelpSurfaceTests` asserts the help text\n83\t   contains the eight spec-section-16 flags and none of `--lab-id`, `--model`,\n84\t   `--test-static`, `--test-simulated-all`, `--test-live-capabilities`,\n85\t   `--test-golden-l01`, `--interrupt-after`, or the removed time-limit flags.\n86\t3. **Mode mutual exclusion, arguments, canonical paths, collision/resume\n87\t   rules, stdout JSON, stderr diagnostics, exit codes.**\n88\t   `ArgumentValidationTests` (mutual exclusion, required-authorization,\n89\t   preflight-rejects-authorization, curriculum file→directory resolution,\n90\t   authorization-file shape validation, collision detection, argparse exit 2);\n91\t   `OutputProjectionTests` (every terminal kind → its section-14 exit code,\n92\t   `accepted_receipt`/`release_receipt` projection, `evidence_index_hash` as a\n93\t   canonical digest over `evidence_index_entries`); `FreshRunWiringTests`\n94\t   (real end-to-end argv → stdout JSON → exit code, one JSON object per\n95\t   invocation, envelope shape, lock released after).\n96\t4. **Preflight is read-only and cannot emit product success.**\n97\t   `PreflightTests` runs `--preflight` against a real, nonexistent output root\n98\t   (real capability probes — this host has `codex`/`gemini`/`pandoc`/`typst`/\n99\t   poppler installed, so the evidence file\n100\t   `results/evidence/N40_CLI_CUTOVER/preflight_read_only.txt` shows a genuine\n101\t   `\"ready\": true` with all six capabilities `PASS`) and asserts the output\n102\t   root still does not exist afterward, the payload's `kind` is `PREFLIGHT`\n103\t   and never `UNIT_ACCEPTED`/`COMPLETE`, and a preflight against a non-empty\n104\t   root reports the collision without touching a byte of it.\n105\t5. **CLI code contains no product nodes, guards, joins, acceptance, or\n106\t   frontier selection.** `test_no_product_node_or_guard_identifiers_appear_in_source`\n107\t   regex-scans the entire file for any `D\\d\\d*`/`M0[1-8]*` token and asserts\n108\t   none exist; `test_only_two_narrow_pure_helpers_are_imported_from_nodes_inputs`\n109\t   and `test_no_import_from_any_other_nodes_or_routing_or_workbook_module` pin\n110\t   the one declared exception (see below) and reject every other import from\n111\t   `nodes.*`, `routing`, `workbook`, `unit_graph`, `model_nodes`, `repair`.\n112\t6. **Missing authorization/capability fails before transmission and never\n113\t   simulates.** `CapabilityAndAuthorizationFailureTests` monkeypatches\n114\t   `transport.prove_transport_capabilities` to raise and asserts the stub\n115\t   compiled graph's `invoke` is **never called**, the process exits 20, and the\n116\t   printed `terminal.kind` is `SYSTEM_FAILURE`; a missing `--authorization`\n117\t   file fails before `build_curriculum_factory_graph` is even called (exit 2,\n118\t   no `terminal` key at all — never a fabricated one).\n119\t7. **Existing Plan 25 roots are readable history but refused for Plan 26\n120\t   resume.** `Plan25ResumeRefusalTests` builds a `checkpoints/0001.json`-shaped\n121\t   legacy root (no `.langgraph/`), runs `--resume` against it, and asserts the\n122\t   graph builder is never called, exit is 3, and the root's file set and bytes\n123\t   are **byte-identical** before and after — the identity-envelope check\n124\t   (`P.read_identity_envelope`) runs before the execution lock is even\n125\t   acquired, so a doomed resume leaves zero filesystem footprint. See\n126\t   `results/evidence/N40_CLI_CUTOVER/plan25_resume_refusal.txt`.\n127\t8. **Production import audit rejects LangChain wrappers/provider SDKs/direct\n128\t   model HTTP.** `test_no_langchain_provider_sdk_or_direct_http_imports`\n129\t   scans every import in the file against `langchain`, `openai`, `anthropic`,\n130\t   `google.generativeai`, `requests`, `httpx`, `urllib3`; none appear. The\n131\t   full, regenerated import list is `results/evidence/N40_CLI_CUTOVER/import_audit.txt`\n132\t   (20 imports total, all stdlib or `runtime.langgraph_factory.*`).\n133\t\n134\t## The one declared exception to \"no node-body imports\"\n135\t\n136\t`_resolve_active_manifest` and `_frozen_input_records`\n137\t(`runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.inputs`) are imported and called once each,\n138\tbefore the graph exists, to fix the identity seed\n139\t(`persistence.prepare_episode_invocation`'s `active_manifest_path`) and the\n140\tauthorization/transport `curriculum_digest` a `RuntimeContext` needs before its\n141\tfirst invocation. Both are pure, side-effect-free hashing/selection functions —\n142\tnot a node body, not a guard, not a routing or acceptance decision. The graph's\n143\town input-freezing node independently recomputes the same values inside the\n144\tepisode and is the sole authority the graph trusts; a drift between the CLI's\n145\tpre-computed digest and the graph's own recomputed one fails closed (an\n146\tauthorization/curriculum-digest mismatch), it never succeeds silently. Reusing\n147\tthe functions, rather than re-implementing the hashing rule a second time, is\n148\twhat keeps the two computations from silently drifting apart.\n149\t\n150\t## Commands\n151\t\n152\t```\n153\t{python} -m pytest -q tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py\n154\t# 72 passed\n155\t```\n156\t\n157\t## Hashes\n158\t\n159\t| Path | sha256 |\n160\t|---|---|\n161\t| `runtime/run_curriculum.py` | `76da9110121ede62a64f29585b840ac934828b41a6376831a355fa95519ec170` |\n162\t| `tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py` | `8d627b17176fb761c765aa32b8c0804958920335b15ee4b273731f9884f58f46` |\n163\t| `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py` (unchanged, inherited from N32) | `eae00c21bfe55ce6e2d6c4374611db4d84d286218d498fa520e799288e152e26` |\n164\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50bcfa3d-b3df-45db-ab55-346f882745b2","uuid":"11316480-950c-4951-ad9c-372a07644119","timestamp":"2026-08-12T18:08:26.154Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/.plan26-run/plan26/attempts/N40_CLI_CUTOVER/attempt-20260812T180522.724742Z-82022fe842/repo/plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/N40_CLI_CUTOVER.result.v1.md","content":"# N40_CLI_CUTOVER result\n\nstatus: PASSED\nnode_prompt: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompts/N40_cli_cutover.prompt.v1.md\npredecessor: N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS (compact state supplied by the controller, status PASSED)\ngeneration: 1\n\n## What this node built\n\n- `runtime/run_curriculum.py` — rewritten from the Plan 25 `CurriculumRuntime`/\n  `CurriculumFa